  "note": "Polled Wednesday 18 May 1955; sixteen candidates for the twelve councillorships (the three aldermen elected in 1952 held their seats for a further three years: Portadown Times, 6 May 1955, p. 1). All ten Unionist candidates were elected, with H. McCourt (Independent, ex-serviceman) and T. Newell (Labour). Labels as printed: U Unionist, L Labour (the Northern Whig: Northern Ireland Labour Party), I Independent. The Northern Whig gives R. J. Williamson and R. Corken."
